Verse 1:
[D]Lord God, [G/B]Your [A]love [F#m]has [G]called [A7]us [Bm]here,
[Em]As we, [A]by [Em/G]love, [Bm]for [D/A]love [A]were [D]made.
[D]Your living [G/B]likeness still [A]we [Bm]bear
[Em]Tho'marred, [D]dishonored, [F#m]disobeyed.
[D]We come, with [F#m/C#]all [Bm]our heart [Em]and [A]mind
[Em/B]Your call [D/A]to [Em/G]hear, [Bm]Your [F#m]love [A7]to [D]find.

Verse 2:
[D]We come [G/B]with [A]self [F#m]inflicted [Bm]pains
[Em]Of broken trust [Bm]and [D/A]chosen wrong,
[D]Half free, [G/B]half [A]bound [D]by [G]inner [Bm]chains,
[Em]By social [A]forces [F#m]swept [G]along,
[D]By powers [F#m/C#]and systems [Bm]close [Em]confined,
[Em/B]Yet seeking hope [Bm]for [F#m]human [D]kind.

Verse 3:
[D]Lord God, [G/B]in [A]Christ [F#m]You [G]call [A7]our [Bm]name,
[Em]And then [A]receive [Bm]us [D/A]as [A]Your [D]own,
[D]Not thro' [G/B]some [A]merit, [G]right, [A]or [Bm]claim,
[Em]But by [D]Your [A]gracious [F#m]love [G]alone.
[D]We strain to [F#m/C#]glimpse [Bm]Your mercy [A]seat,
[Em/B]And find [D/A]You [Em/G]kneeling [F#m]at [A7]our [D]feet.

Verse 4:
[D]Then take the [G/B]towel, [F#m]and [G]break [A7]the [Bm]bread,
[Em]And humble us, [Bm]and [D/A]call [A]us [D]friends.
[D]Suffer [G/B]and [A]serve [D]till [G]all [A]are [Bm]fed
[Em]And show [D]how [A]grandly [F#m]love [G]intends
[D]To work till [F#m]all [Bm]creation [A]sings,
[Em/B]To fill [D/A]all [Em/G]worlds, [Bm]to [F#m]crown [A7]all [D]things.

Verse 5:
[D]Lord God, [G/B]in [A]Christ [F#m]You [G]set [A7]us [Bm]free
[Em]Your life [A]to [Em/G]live, [Bm]Your [D/A]joy [A]to [D]share.
[D]Give us [G/B]Your [A]Spirit's [G]liberty
[Em]To turn [D]from [A]guilt [Bm]and [F#m]dull [G]despair
[D]And offer [F#m/C#]all [Bm]that faith [Em]can [A]do,
[Em/B]While [D/A]love [Em/G]is [Bm]making [F#m]all [A7]things [D]new.
